      "source": [
        "## Create a Reliable Test Set\n",
        "\n",
        "### Subtask:\n",
        "Implement and execute the code for splitting the dataset using simple random hold-out and stratified sampling. Present the proportion checks and the answers to the questions regarding test set generation, 'seed', and stratified sampling effectiveness.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4fec960c"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "First, I will import `train_test_split`, create the `income_cat` attribute on the main `housing` DataFrame, then perform a simple random split. The `income_cat` column will be used for comparison and then dropped from the simple random split sets.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "1efbb885",
        "outputId": "76ce30d3-fefe-4113-c799-36e1ed23ccf1"
      },
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create income category attribute\n",
        "housing[\"income_cat\"] = pd.cut(housing[\"median_income\"],\n",
        "                               bins=[0., 1.5, 3.0, 4.5, 6., np.inf],\n",
        "                               labels=[1, 2, 3, 4, 5])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Income categories created and added to housing DataFrame.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Simple random sampling\n",
        "train_set, test_set = train_test_split(housing, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nSimple random split completed.\")\n",
        "print(f\"Train set size: {len(train_set)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Test set size: {len(test_set)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Drop income_cat from the simple random split sets to revert to original form for other tasks\n",
        "train_set_random = train_set.drop(\"income_cat\", axis=1)\n",
        "test_set_random = test_set.drop(\"income_cat\", axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n'income_cat' column dropped from simple random split train and test sets.\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 10,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Income categories created and added to housing DataFrame.\n",
            "\n",
            "Simple random split completed.\n",
            "Train set size: 16512\n",
            "Test set size: 4128\n",
            "\n",
            "'income_cat' column dropped from simple random split train and test sets.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "86d58355"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "I will perform stratified sampling using `StratifiedShuffleSplit` on the `housing` DataFrame, ensuring the income categories are well-represented in both the training and test sets. Afterward, I will drop the temporary `income_cat` column from the stratified sets.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "713daed3",
        "outputId": "ad2289ac-dd31-40c9-b1d7-be49d6c23483"
      },
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedShuffleSplit\n",
        "\n",
        "split = StratifiedShuffleSplit(n_splits=1, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
        "for train_index, test_index in split.split(housing, housing[\"income_cat\"]):\n",
        "    strat_train_set = housing.loc[train_index]\n",
        "    strat_test_set = housing.loc[test_index]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Stratified sampling completed.\")\n",
        "print(f\"Stratified Train set size: {len(strat_train_set)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Stratified Test set size: {len(strat_test_set)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Drop income_cat from the stratified split sets\n",
        "strat_train_set = strat_train_set.drop(\"income_cat\", axis=1)\n",
        "strat_test_set = strat_test_set.drop(\"income_cat\", axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Also drop income_cat from the original housing DataFrame now that it's no longer needed for splitting\n",
        "housing_original_income_cat = housing[\"income_cat\"].copy() # Keep a copy for proportion check\n",
        "housing.drop(\"income_cat\", axis=1, inplace=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    \"\\n'income_cat' column dropped from stratified train/test sets and original housing DataFrame.\"\n",
        ")\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Stratified sampling completed.\n",
            "Stratified Train set size: 16512\n",
            "Stratified Test set size: 4128\n",
            "\n",
            "'income_cat' column dropped from stratified train/test sets and original housing DataFrame.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
