        "By comparing the proportions, we can see that the **Stratified Test Set** proportions are remarkably close to the **Original Dataset (Full)** proportions for each income category. For instance, the difference in proportion for category 1 is 0.039826 vs 0.039971 (very small), for category 2 it's 0.318847 vs 0.318798 (also very small), and so on. In contrast, the **Simple Random Test Set** shows slightly larger deviations from the original proportions (e.g., category 2: 0.318847 vs 0.324370; category 4: 0.176308 vs 0.167393). This clearly demonstrates that stratified sampling successfully maintained the income category distribution across the test set, ensuring it is representative of the overall dataset, which was the expected outcome."
